    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Change\n\nRejecting owner creation with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`CityCapacityExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` in the `rest.advice` package, following the same pattern as the existing `DuplicateHouseholdException`/`DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception mapping it to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409), producing a `ProblemDetail` consistent with the other duplicate/conflict handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (the sole controller with `addOwner`) \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant and, in `addOwner`, a guard that throws `CityCapacityExceededException` when `countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= 50`. It reuses the pre-existing case-insensitive `countOwnersInCity` helper and runs right after field normalization so the check sees the canonical city.\n\n### Tests\n- The provided acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to get 409) passes.\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.\n\nThe check uses `>= 50` so that when a city holds exactly 50 owners the next create is rejected, matching the spec (\"already contains 50 or more owners\") and the test's fill-to-50-then-51st-rejected scenario.",
